{"id": "21587", "revid": "2253620", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=21587", "title": "Mason (Ohio)", "text": "Mason is a suburb north of Cincinnati in Warren County, Ohio.\nGet in.\nBy car.\nFrom Interstate I-71 northbound, take Ohio Exit 24 (Western Row Road/Kings Island). At the end of the exit ramp, turn left (West) on Western Row Road/Tylersville Road. Stay right on the three lane road to stay on Tylersville Road. At the intersection of Tylersville Road with Mason-Montgomer Road, turn right (north). One mile north, Mason-Montgomery Road intersects with Main Street (State Route 42). You are now in downtown Mason, Ohio.\nFrom Interstate I-71 southbound, take the Kings Mills Road exit. Kings Mills Road west. At a T-intersection, Route 741 turns north, Kings Mills turns south. Kings Mills Road curves through a residential neighborhood before turning back to the west. Kings Mills Ts into Main Street (State Route 42). Turn left (west) on Main Street about 3 blocks to the intersection of Main Street with Mason-Montgomery Road. You are in downtown Mason, Ohio.\nFrom Interstate I-75, take the Tylersville Road exit. Drive east to the intersection of Mason-Montgomery Road with Tylersville Road. Turn left (north) onto Mason-Montgomery Road. One mile north, Mason-Montgomery Road intersects with Main Street (State Route 42). You are now in downtown Mason, Ohio.\nBy bus.\nSORTA, Southwest Ohio Regional Transit Authority[dead link], provides bus service from downtown Cincinnati to a parking lot at Western Row Road and Columbia Road and along Bus Route 71/72 (I-71/Columbia Road/Montgomery Road/Fields Ertel Road).\nBy plane.\nMason served by three major airports:\nEach airport can be accessed from Mason with at least some portion of interstate driving.\nEstimated driving time from Mason to the airports are:\nStay safe.\nBe alert for drunk drivers on the weekend."}
{"id": "21588", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=21588", "title": "Mason City", "text": "\"For other places with the same name, see (disambiguation).\"\nMason City is a city in Iowa, renowned for its collection of architecture by Frank Lloyd Wright and other Prairie School architects, considered the most significant concentration of such architecture outside of Oak Park, Illinois.\nGet in.\nBy car.\nU.S. Highways 18 and 65 go through Mason City. Interstate 35 runs through the nearby town of Clear Lake, about 7 miles west of Mason City.\nGet around.\nPublic transportation is close to non-existent in Mason City. There is a paratransit van service available but no public bus system in place.\nEat.\nThe Northwestern Steakhouse is locally famous for its steaks. Birdsall's ice cream is also locally well-known for its delicious shakes, malts, and ice cream and is a local landmark, unchanged for decades."}
